/target

# The Windows package identity Partner Center assigned. Not a credential —
# `Publisher` is in the manifest of every package the Store distributes, and the
# store id is in the public listing URL — but it is an account's identifiers on
# a public record, which is the judgement `slipcase-desktop` made for its copy
# and this is the same one. `identity.psd1.example` beside it is committed and
# says what goes in.
/packaging/windows/identity.psd1

# A Microsoft Store submission walkthrough, if one is written here. It would
# name the store id and whatever the submission API is given, and
# `packaging/windows/README.md` is where everything that belongs on a public
# record goes instead.
/packaging/windows/SUBMITTING.local.md

# Built packages, the staging tree they come from, and the throwaway
# certificate. All of it is assembled by `packaging/windows/build-msix.ps1` from
# what is committed, and none of it is reproducible byte-for-byte anyway: a
# rebuild of identical source differs in the COFF and debug timestamps and the
# PDB GUID, which is why that script makes the upload and the local copy from
# one staging tree rather than from two builds.
/dist/
